From a8394a11fd4904760a575ebb176fa54bc9e05287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verify-local <verify@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 04:27:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vm: pre-flight llm check on run()/resume_with_program() (Q2)

- ExecutionVM.__init__: llm now Optional[LLMAdapter] = None (already on
  origin via 4acf83c's runtime-only check inside _execute_llm; this commit
  moves the rejection point).
- New ExecutionVM._require_llm_if_needed(program): rejects before any step
  executes if the program declares any type=llm step and no adapter is
  configured. Deliberately over-approximates reachability. Raises VMError
  directly (VM-misconfiguration precondition, same class as ResumeError),
  not a Trace(FAILED).
- Called from both run() and resume_with_program(), before either touches
  state/cursor_repo. Backstop check inside _execute_llm kept as-is.
- tests/test_llm_optional.py: 6 tests -- tool-only happy path, mixed-program
  control (succeeds with adapter), pre-flight zero-side-effects, pre-flight
  on a structurally-unreachable llm step, pre-flight on resume() before
  cursor load, backstop unit on _execute_llm directly.
- tests/test_cancellation.py: docstring no longer points at an external
  DECISIONS.md entry the reader can't see; rationale inlined.
- CHANGELOG.md: [Unreleased] section -- Changed/Added/Fixed/Note.

Gate: ruff clean, mypy 0/14, pytest 499/499 (493 + 6 new).
Negative controls performed (not committed): reverting either the run() or
the resume_with_program() call to _require_llm_if_needed independently
made exactly the corresponding new test fail (DID NOT RAISE), with no
effect on the other tests.
